# Agent commit-signing keys. Public keys only — safe to commit, and this file is
# the repository's record of which key belongs to which agent.
#
# All three agents push as one GitHub identity, so a Co-Authored-By trailer is
# only as trustworthy as the agent typing it. A signature is not: producing one
# requires the private key. That makes authorship auditable rather than merely
# asserted, which is what rule 5 (the author never merges its own PR) rests on.
#
# Verify locally with:  scripts/agent-verify-signatures
# Register each public key on GitHub as a *signing* key so commits show Verified.
#
# Add your line when you generate a key:
#   scripts/agent-signing-setup <agent>
claude ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAILE8TZVuwwCNWFseQdD98AkxCs6qqiA37YkPoHMlnLxI eth402-agent-claude
